# Backup files (CLAUDE.md Rule #1)
*.backup
*.bak
*-FINAL.*
*-old.*
# `*.backup` does NOT match `server.js.backup-2025-07-07` — anything after
# `.backup` defeats it. That gap let three ~260 KB copies of server.js get
# committed in Jul 2025; they rode every Heroku slug and were downloadable over
# plain HTTP until express.static('.') was removed on 2026-07-29. Deleted in
# fe3dd77 (recoverable: git show 9b84e6f:server.js.backup-with-comments).
*.backup-*
*-backup
*-backup.*
#
# DELIBERATELY NOT LISTED — do not "complete" this list without re-checking:
#   *-fixed.*  3 legitimate tracked test files use it
#              (tests/manual/test-fixed-endpoints.js and two others).
#   *-FIXED.*  core.ignorecase is TRUE on the Windows checkout and FALSE on
#              Heroku's Linux build, so the uppercase form silently behaves as
#              the lowercase one locally — a file ignored on one machine and
#              committed from another.
#   *-v2.*     a real version convention here, not a lazy copy
#              (scripts/aggregate-industry-lookalikes-v2.js).

